        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(config): support externally managed GitOps config",
        "body": "Closes #103606\n\nRelated: #55753, #59616, #83851, #89526\n\nPrior related PRs: #90653, #96438\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nKubernetes and GitOps operators currently have to choose between mounting an\nexternally owned config as mutable local state or replacing the pod when a\nConfigMap generation changes. That makes safe config changes drop active\nsessions and lets OpenClaw write back into a source whose desired state belongs\nto Flux, Argo CD, Nix, or another controller.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a host-only `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_MANAGED=1` ownership contract: OpenClaw\ncontinues to read and reconcile the config, but all config-writing CLI and\nGateway surfaces reject before side effects. The Gateway watches both the\nconfigured path and its bounded parent, reconciles Kubernetes AtomicWriter\nsymlink swaps in process, and keeps its diff baseline at the last successfully\napplied generation so failed, ignored, and restart-pending generations cannot\npoison later reload decisions.\n\nThe Kubernetes example now mounts a stable, read-only ConfigMap directory at\n`/etc/openclaw-config`, keeps runtime state on the PVC, and avoids a config hash\nrollout trigger. Nix keeps its existing ownership/error contract. General\n`$include` dependency watching and a transactional redesign of OpenClaw's own\ninternal config-write pipeline are intentionally out of scope; settings already\nclassified as restart-required still use the normal lifecycle restart path.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGitOps-managed pods can apply hot-safe root config changes without restarting\nthe pod, preserving active sessions and in-memory state. Operators get a clear,\nconsistent `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_MANAGED` error from setup, config, agent, skill, and\nplugin mutation surfaces instead of a late filesystem failure. Invalid external\ngenerations leave the last applied runtime active until the controller publishes\na valid replacement.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AWS Crabbox `cbx_cace403c44f7` (released), exact rebased head:\n  - `run_d7143581a688`: 1,095 focused assertions passed across 9 Vitest shards,\n    including real AtomicWriter `..data` swaps and an out-of-parent symlink target.\n  - `run_853f68350f67`: `pnpm check:changed` passed core/core-test typechecks,\n    sharded lint, script lint, dependency/boundary guards, and import-cycle checks.\n  - `run_8437bd887cb6`: production `pnpm build` passed.\n  - `run_39871951e7c7`: Docker config-reload E2E passed (build, live Gateway,\n    config mutation, post-write RPC, and reload-log verification).\n  - `run_91fc242014fc`, `run_f372aee1e015`, `run_be7307e8255b`: docs MDX,\n    5,804 internal links, and docs formatting passed.\n- `bash -n scripts/k8s/deploy.sh`, `kubectl kustomize scripts/k8s/manifests`,\n  and `git diff --check` passed locally.\n- Fresh autoreview completed clean after the final post-rebase integration fix.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and review.\n",
